Start with the sidebar collapsed on a narrow screen.

The layout has no media queries and #side is a fixed 248px, so on a phone-width
viewport the sidebar takes most of the window and the 3D map is left with a strip
too narrow to read — 164px of 412px on a Pixel-sized screen. The map is the
point of the app, and a first-time visitor on a phone sees mostly filter
controls.

The header toggle already exists and #side.hidden already works, so this only
decides the initial state: collapsed below 700px, unchanged above it, and one tap
brings the sidebar back. Applied before the first resize() so the canvas is
measured at its full width from the start.

diff --git a/index.html b/index.html
index 78595d7..184d2c6 100644
--- a/index.html
+++ b/index.html
@@ -2377,6 +2377,9 @@ async function loadOfferedSnapshot(){
 }
 
 (async function boot(){
+  // The sidebar is a fixed 248px, which on a phone leaves almost no map. Start it
+  // collapsed on a narrow screen; the toggle in the header brings it back.
+  if (window.innerWidth < 700) $("side").classList.add("hidden");
   resize();
   try {
     await idb.open();
